SECTION 2 — FREE LICENSE AND COMMON OPERATING PERMISSIONS
================================================================================

2.1  Subject to this License, the Copyright Holder grants a worldwide,
     non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license
     to obtain the Software from Official Distribution Channels and reproduce,
     install, execute, display, and use it solely for Permitted Free Use.
     Commercial rights arise only under Section 5 and a License Confirmation.

2.2  Both free use and licensed commercial use allow the copies reasonably
     necessary for the permitted scope: production where authorized, development,
     local machines, staging, preview, QA, CI, disaster recovery, backups,
     replicas, and migrations. These environments and their servers are not
     separately charged. An environment labeled "test" that actually serves
     live customers must have the rights required for that production use.

2.3  You may style, theme, configure, and integrate the Software in a permitted
     application, including application CSS/Blade overrides and Browser Assets.
     You need not display a public "Powered by Flex Fields" badge. Retain the
     copyright/license notices in code and distributed assets where present;
     ordinary application branding does not authorize relabeling the Software.

2.4  You may inspect, patch, adapt, and privately fork the Software for Your
     permitted scope, including changes under vendor/. Private package feeds
     for Authorized Personnel or Covered Entities are permitted under Section
     1.5(b). Modifications do not enlarge the license, remove attribution, or
     authorize public forks or external redistribution. Support for modifications
     is not promised. Contributions follow Section 4.

2.5  There are no developer-seat, user, tenant, server, CPU, region, or revenue
     limits for a use otherwise within the applicable grant. Unlimited scale
     does not expand the number of Products or entities licensed, authorize
     Customer Installations, or grant redistribution or sublicensing rights.

