SECTION 3 — RESTRICTIONS APPLYING TO EVERY PLAN
================================================================================

3.1  No license is granted beyond the rights expressly stated in Sections 2
     and 5 and the applicable License Confirmation. Single Product, Unlimited
     Company, and Enterprise Group are "Standard Plans." Their additional
     commercial grant is limited to Section 5.1 and their respective scope.
     Merely holding a commercial license does not waive this Section 3.

3.2  Except for Section 1.5's limited exceptions or express Custom rights, You
     may not redistribute, sell, sublicense, publish, mirror, or transfer the
     Software or a Derivative Work, alone or inside a Bundled Product. This
     includes public/private customer repositories, package feeds, email copies,
     source handovers, downloadable builds, and Customer Installations. The
     restriction applies even if the Software is incidental, encrypted, compiled,
     supplied without a separate charge, or customers promise not to extract it.

3.3  Standard Plans do not authorize selling or distributing templates, starter
     kits, boilerplates, SDKs, component libraries, or reusable application source
     incorporating or commercially requiring the Software. Requiring the buyer
     to fetch it from official channels does not by itself authorize that
     distribution business. Genuine bespoke client development with direct
     licensing is separately permitted under Section 5.6.

3.4  Standard Plans do not authorize white-label/OEM arrangements in which
     another business receives the Software or independent rights to operate,
     resell, or sublicense a Software-based product as its own. Cosmetic SaaS
     tenant branding and ordinary referrals are permitted under Sections 1.10,
     1.12, and 5.1; white-label product distribution or reseller operating rights
     require an express Custom agreement.

3.5  You may not market the Software or a Derivative Work as Your own field
     library, UI kit, plugin, or substantially substitutable developer toolkit
     without express Custom rights. A hosted business application, including a
     hosted form builder, is not prohibited merely because it uses the Software's
     fields extensively, if users receive Runtime Access/ordinary output only.
     Exporting reusable Software code or supplying a competing component kit
     requires Custom rights. Independently developed code containing no protected
     Software material is not claimed by this License.

3.6  Preserve copyright, license, and third-party notices. Do not misrepresent
     authorship or use the Copyright Holder's trademarks to imply endorsement.
     Renaming or rebranding the Software itself requires express Custom rights;
     those rights do not implicitly transfer copyright or permit false authorship.

3.7  Do not assign, sell, lend, pool, share, or sublicense license rights except
     as expressly permitted in Section 5. End users may use Your application
     under Your own terms, but receive no independent Software rights from You.
     Separate purchases may legitimately cover separate Products/entities; they
     cannot be pooled to create redistribution rights or an unlicensed group.

3.8  Do not evade scope limits by changing names, splitting vendor files from a
     downloadable product, using intermediaries, or describing Software delivery
     as hosting. Classification follows the actual ownership, operation,
     deliverables, and rights, not invoice wording or package format.

3.9  Mandatory-law rights, including any non-waivable rights to necessary backup,
     observation, study, testing, interoperability, or lawful transfer, are not
     excluded. This License does not grant other uses beyond its express scope.

