SECTION 5 — COMMERCIAL PLANS AND COMMERCIAL LIFECYCLE
================================================================================

5.1  COMMON STANDARD GRANT. Once effective under Section 5.7, a Standard Plan
     grants worldwide, non-exclusive commercial rights to reproduce, install,
     run, modify, and integrate the Software in Products within its scope, and
     to sell subscriptions or other Runtime Access to those Products in Hosted
     Use. Section 2's operating permissions also apply. You must own the Product
     (excluding third-party dependencies) and operate it directly or through
     Authorized Personnel; Enterprise Group permits ownership/operation by its
     Covered Entities collectively. A mere license to resell another owner's
     Product is not Product ownership for these plans.
     All Standard Plans include unlimited users, tenants, Authorized Personnel,
     and environments for covered Products. Custom domains, tenant logos/colors,
     separate tenant databases, and dedicated instances remain covered when
     You retain the Product and service relationship and grant no independent
     reseller rights. Neither a Standard Plan nor a large customer count
     authorizes Customer Installations, Software redistribution, or OEM rights.

5.2  SINGLE PRODUCT — USD 249, ONE-TIME CURRENT LIST PRICE.
     One named natural person or legal entity may use the Software in one
     named Product, including all its permitted versions and environments.
     The Product is identified in the License Confirmation before commercial
     deployment. You may develop its features and replace its brand without
     buying again; record a changed name with the Copyright Holder by email.
     A separately offered Product requires another Single Product license or
     an upgrade. Retiring a Product does not free a reusable license slot.
     No other legal entity is covered except as Authorized Personnel working
     solely for the named licensee. A Product sale follows Section 5.10.

5.3  UNLIMITED COMPANY — USD 699, ONE-TIME CURRENT LIST PRICE.
     One named natural person operating as a sole proprietor, or one named
     legal entity, may use the Software in unlimited current and future Products
     it owns and operates. Multiple brands, departments, employees, and teams
     within that entity are included. A founder's separate company, parent,
     subsidiary, sister company, client, or joint venture is not included.
     There is no group extension by shared ownership, billing, domain, office,
     or development team. Other entities need their own applicable grants or
     coverage under Enterprise Group or an express Custom agreement.

5.4  ENTERPRISE GROUP — USD 1,499, ONE-TIME CURRENT LIST PRICE.
     The named parent and its Covered Entities may use the Software across
     unlimited Products owned/operated within that group, including shared
     development teams, internal hosting, and private repositories. This is a
     direct extension of the Copyright Holder's grant to qualifying entities,
     administered by the parent, not a general right to sublicense.
     (a) The parent must have authority to accept for Covered Entities and
         remains responsible for group compliance. Each participating entity
         must comply with this License.
     (b) Current and future wholly owned subsidiaries qualify automatically
         while Section 1.14 is satisfied, without a per-subsidiary fee. Keep
         an up-to-date list and notify the Copyright Holder of changes within
         thirty (30) calendar days. Notification is administrative, not a
         separate purchase or discretionary approval requirement.
     (c) An entity leaving the group may continue only its existing deployments
         for ninety (90) calendar days after departure, solely to transition
         to its own license or remove the Software. It may maintain/security-
         patch those deployments but may not launch new Products or redistribute
         the Software under this transition. At its end, separate rights are
         required. The parent's remaining covered use continues.
     (d) Partial ownership, joint ventures, and entities outside the named
         parent's qualifying chain require separate licenses or an expressly
         negotiated extension; "Enterprise" alone does not include them.
     (e) Covered entities may exchange copies for covered use. Delivery to
         external customers still requires Custom rights. Enterprise Group
         contains no OEM, customer-installation, or external redistribution grant.

5.5  CUSTOM / OEM / REDISTRIBUTION — QUOTATIONS START AT USD 2,999.
     A separate written agreement is required for Customer Installations,
     distribution of Products containing or commercially requiring the Software,
     OEM, resale, developer kits, Software white-labeling, or sublicensing beyond
     Standard Plans. The starting price is an entry point for a narrowly scoped
     agreement, not a flat price for all rights, an automatic license, or a cap.
     No particular Custom right is included until expressly written into the
     agreement. A quote must identify:
     (a) licensees, Products, Software versions, and permitted modifications;
     (b) delivery methods, installation/customer limits, territories, channels,
         and the duration of the grant;
     (c) downstream runtime/source/modification rights, attribution, and any
         permitted further sublicensing or distribution;
     (d) applicable fees: one-time, per-installation, royalty, revenue share,
         recurring minimums, or another expressly agreed basis;
     (e) any reporting, support, update entitlement, and treatment of deployed
         customer copies at expiry or termination.
     Copyright ownership, exclusivity, public registry publication, unlimited
     downstream use, and direct support of Your customers are not included by
     implication. Requests may be declined. Non-standard group coverage can also
     be negotiated; this does not itself confer any redistribution rights.

5.6  AGENCIES, CONTRACTORS, AND DIRECT CLIENT LICENSES.
     (a) A genuine client-owned bespoke application may be developed and
         maintained by its agency as Authorized Personnel of that client. The
         client obtains the Software directly from Official Distribution Channels
         and relies on its own Permitted Free Use or commercial grant. The agency
         may install it into the client's controlled environment on that client's
         behalf and access that environment solely to provide services.
     (b) The agency may deliver its independently written application code without
         Software copies and identify the official dependency. This exception
         applies to bespoke development for the identified owner, not resale of
         the agency's reusable product, template, boilerplate, or customer edition.
         It does not sublicense the agency's license or transfer its private fork.
     (c) A client's own internal application can therefore qualify for free use;
         a client-owned SaaS requires that client's suitable Standard Plan for
         Hosted Use. The agency's Unlimited Company never covers client-owned
         Products. The client needs Custom rights if it subsequently distributes
         Software-containing Products to its own customers.
     (d) Selling or installing Your own product for many customers is not converted
         into bespoke development by separate invoices or customer downloads
         from Packagist. That model requires Custom authorization for the vendor.
         Customer licenses alone do not confer distribution rights on the vendor.

5.7  FORMATION, PAYMENT, AND PRECEDENCE.
     (a) Before payment, the order must identify the licensee, plan/scope,
         applicable License version, price, taxes where applicable, and any
         departures from standard terms. These terms must be available to the
         purchaser before acceptance. A later email cannot unilaterally reduce
         the accepted grant.
     (b) Commercial rights become effective when payment is confirmed and the
         Copyright Holder issues/authenticates the License Confirmation, unless
         that instrument expressly agrees a different payment/effective date.
         Keep both confirmation and payment record. A donation, unaccepted quote,
         public price listing, or unsupported payment is not a commercial grant.
     (c) Priority is: an expressly agreed Custom agreement/amendment; the accepted
         License Confirmation for its named scope and commercial particulars;
         the applicable version of this LICENSE; then the matching COMMERCIAL.md
         guide for explanation. A routine Standard Plan confirmation cannot
         silently add redistribution rights. Such rights require express Custom
         terms identifying the relevant exception.
     (d) The USD amounts above are this version's public list prices, excluding
         applicable VAT/sales tax. Actual taxes/currency and the final amount
         must be disclosed in the quote/checkout. New public prices may change
         for future orders; accepted orders and issued grants are unaffected.
         No subsequent price increase creates a balance due on a paid license.

5.8  DURATION, VERSIONS, UPDATES, AND SUPPORT.
     Standard Plans are perpetual within the licensed scope, subject to their
     conditions and Section 7. No annual fee, per-user royalty, or renewal is
     required to continue that use. To the extent permitted by law, the Copyright
     Holder will not terminate a paid Standard Plan merely for convenience.
     The grant covers the package version obtained and subsequent updates,
     including major versions of this same package, released by the Copyright
     Holder through Official Distribution Channels. Those updates may be used
     under the issued commercial grant; a new embedded license text does not
     reduce it without agreement. Separate products/add-ons are excluded.
     Current source and releases are available through public official channels.
     Payment buys usage rights, not a private update subscription. There is no
     promise to create future releases, maintain public hosting indefinitely,
     support every framework version, supply fixes by a deadline, or provide an
     SLA. You may retain permitted copies. Discontinuation or choosing not to
     update does not end perpetual rights to versions already covered.
     Support, customization, training, indemnities, and service commitments are
     included only when expressly agreed. Custom duration/updates follow its
     agreement. No runtime activation or periodic online validation is required
     by the Standard Plans; lack of a technical check does not expand rights.

5.9  STANDARD PLAN UPGRADES.
     For licenses originally issued under version 2.0, the holder may request
     an upgrade from Single Product to Unlimited Company or Enterprise Group,
     or from Unlimited Company to Enterprise Group. There is no upgrade deadline.
     The upgrade fee is the then-current destination list price minus eligible
     net license fees already paid, with a minimum of zero. Eligible credit
     excludes taxes, refunds, chargebacks, support, and Custom fees; it cannot
     be redeemed for cash or used twice. Several lower-tier grants may be
     consolidated only if all their Products/entities fit the destination scope,
     their holders consent, and the grants are identified in the new confirmation.
     Upgraded grants are replaced, not retained as transferable spare licenses.
     Consolidation does not authorize historical out-of-scope use. Custom and
     pre-2.0 upgrade credits require an individual written quote; there is no
     automatic downgrade refund or Custom credit. The expanded scope starts
     only when the upgrade is paid and confirmed under Section 5.7.

5.10 OWNERSHIP CHANGES AND TRANSFERS.
     A change of trading name or shareholders does not transfer a license if
     the same legal licensee remains and scope conditions continue. Notify the
     Copyright Holder of legal-name/contact changes. Under Enterprise Group,
     acquisition of the named parent does not automatically cover the acquirer's
     other entities; subsidiary departures follow Section 5.4(c).
     A sale of a Product, assignment to another company, incorporation of a sole
     proprietorship, or merger into a different legal entity does not automatically
     transfer rights, except where mandatory law provides otherwise. Obtain
     written transfer approval, appropriate new licenses, or an agreed transition
     before the recipient begins using the Software under the transferred scope.
     The Copyright Holder may agree a Single Product transfer with its entire
     Product; it does not carry unrelated portfolio rights. Transfers of Products
     within an existing Enterprise Group remain covered while both entities
     qualify and the Product stays within the group.

5.11 REFUNDS AND REMEDIES.
     Voluntary refunds follow the terms disclosed for the accepted order. Unless
     that order or the payment provider's applicable policy provides otherwise,
     issued commercial grants are non-refundable. Mandatory refund, withdrawal,
     and other statutory rights are preserved. If payment was collected but the
     Copyright Holder declines to issue the agreed grant, the license payment
     must be refunded. A full license refund cancels that commercial grant; a
     partial price adjustment does not unless expressly agreed. A billing dispute
     is not itself a license breach; actual non-payment follows Section 7.

